      "writtenOn": "2018-11-28T00:43:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re going to need to have access to the SN Bits and RMA count on the factory and RMA floors, and also as part of Chrome OS startup (e.g. https://docs.google.com/document/d/1r1lO653UNIDqoj_oVtED5wLQFp5b_4igdVtaA1G25jU/edit#heading\u003dh.f2h7486rvn5s where the idea would be to use, e.g. gsctool -S to see if we have SN Bits that are not simply all f).\n\nIIRC, using tpmc is a bit arcane, but more importantly requires knowing the exact addresses to look at (and maybe some address translation too)? I don\u0027t think that\u0027s something that is friendly for the above use cases. Could this be done inside gsctool instead even without a vendor command? Or would we need a vendor command?",
